# A tenant: a Trusted Domain built from its written spec to a verified
# cluster with ChRIS on it, smoked (docs/stratus.adoc, D14).
#
# The size is the spec's, written before this plays by `cluster new` (or the
# controller's SIZE and COMMIT, which send that line and then this play).
# This file is the procedure, never the shape: spec.yaml stays the truth of
# what a cluster is.
#
# The build asks before the first step that bills. A NO there, or Ctrl-C,
# leaves the build where it stands, and the play stops at the claim that the
# build is done; `play ~/tenant.mise --param NAME=…` again goes on from the
# first step not done.
@name         tenant
@description  Build a Trusted Domain from its spec through ChRIS's smoke journey, and answer its status.
@param        NAME
@answers      TENANT

# Only a cluster built here is built on; an adopted one is planned against.
expect cluster ${NAME} class eq built
cluster build ${NAME}
expect cluster ${NAME} step smoke eq done

# The build's verify step ran the ten checks against the cluster through its
# kubeconfig, which stays on the host, until the new cluster settled.
expect cluster ${NAME} verify eq 10

TENANT=$(cluster ${NAME})
